  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The heading of the Passion. PÁSSIO is the nominative of a heading, with no verb expressed or understood; NOSTRI agrees with DÓMINI, and IESU CHRISTI stands in apposition to it; SECÚNDUM with the accusative names the evangelist. Unlike the other Gospel headings it is printed without the cross.",
    "source": {
      "method": "The Latin follows the Benziger Brothers 1962 editio iuxta typicam, which prints this heading over the Passion on printed p. 139 (IA leaf n218 / PDF p. 219); it is compared with the heading line of the pinned Divinum Officium Palm Sunday file (Tempora/Quad6-0r), in the [Evangelium1] section that its [Evangelium] section calls. Source review remains pending.",
